# The reversible Unicode instruction algebra: assertions,
# inverse operators, and round-trip certificates.
# (Owner's worked examples, in bracket form.)

# Assertions compare value, shape, and kind.
🔺 📏 ➕ [1 2 3] [4 5 6]
>>>>>>>€ [5 7 9]
🔺 🟦 🔄 [[1 2] [3 4]]
>>>>>>>€ [[1 3] [2 4]]
🔺 🔹 ⚖️ 3 3
>>>>>>>€ 👑
🔺 🔹 ⚖️ 3 4
>>>>>>>€ 💀

# ↶ applies the registered inverse: (result, other operand)
# recovers the first operand.
🌀 📏 ➕ [1 2] [3 4]
>>>>>>>€ [4 6]
↶ 🌀 📏 ➕ [4 6] [3 4]
>>>>>>>€ [1 2]

# A forward/inverse assertion pair, certified as a round trip.
🔺 🟦 🔄 [[1 2] [3 4]]
>>>>>>>€ [[1 3] [2 4]]
↶ 🔺 🟦 🔄 [[1 3] [2 4]]
>>>>>>>€ [[1 2] [3 4]]
🛡️ ROUNDTRIP

# ⟲ runs a one-line round trip and returns the recovered operand.
⟲ 🌀 📏 ✖️ [3 5] [2 4]

# Flatten's inverse needs saved metadata; the binding supplies it.
m ← 🔺 🟦 🔄 2 2 1 2 3 4
f ← 🌀 📏 📦 @m
>>>>>>>€ [1 3 2 4]
↶ 🌀 📏 📦 @f
>>>>>>>€ [[1 3] [2 4]]

# Or the metadata is supplied explicitly, via 🗳️ reconstruct.
🌀 🟦 🗳️ 2 2 1 3 2 4
>>>>>>>€ [[1 3] [2 4]]
